# Test: a pushed URL answers a whole page, and both traversals land on one
# VALIDATES: AC-7 -- an htmx navigation pushes a URL, that URL answers a
#            complete page on a direct GET, and the browser's own back and
#            forward buttons render pages rather than fragments
# PREVENTS: the failure htmx 4 makes reachable. htmx 2 keeps a history cache and
#           restores the previous DOM on back, so a pushed URL that answers only
#           a fragment is never noticed. htmx 4 keeps no cache and traverses
#           through the Navigation API: each traversal is a real navigation and
#           the server's answer is what the operator sees.
#
# The finder is the UI that pushes. The workbench renders no hx-push-url at all,
# so a test on the default mode would assert over a page with no history to test.
#
# Every step names a URL the finder actually pushes. It renders 61 of them and
# TestPushedURLsAnswerAFullPage (internal/component/web/handler_history_test.go)
# holds that whole population; this file proves the browser half, which no
# server-side test can reach.

option=server:kind=web
option=env:var=ze.web.ui-mode:value=finder
option=timeout:value=120s

# The pushed URL fetched directly is a whole page: it carries a head that loads
# the library, not a bare fragment served into a page that already had one.
action=open:path=/show/bgp/
expect=head:contains=htmx
expect=element:text=peer

# Now build the history an operator builds. POSITIVE CONTROL: the click issues
# an htmx request and pushes its URL. If htmx were not live the address would
# not change, and both traversals below would be asserting over a page that
# never navigated.
action=open:path=/show/
expect=element:text=bgp
expect=url:not-contains=/show/bgp

action=click:text=bgp
action=wait
expect=url:contains=/show/bgp

# Back is the entry BEHIND: the finder root, whole page, with none of the bgp
# detail on it. htmx 4 keeps no DOM cache, so what lands here is the server's
# answer to a fresh GET of /show/.
action=back
action=wait
expect=url:not-contains=/show/bgp
expect=head:contains=htmx
expect=element:text=bgp

# Forward is the entry AHEAD, and it is a second traversal rather than the
# reverse of the first. The Navigation API replaced popstate in 4.0.0-beta6, so
# this is the direction no jsdom probe could exercise.
action=forward
action=wait
expect=url:contains=/show/bgp
expect=head:contains=htmx
expect=element:text=peer
